# Restart app after functional changes

When you finish implementing or fixing **user-facing behavior** in this repo (UI, tray menu, notifications, weather logic, config that affects runtime, etc.):

1. **Stop** any running instance of WeatherAlert before starting a new one.
2. **Start** the app again so the user can verify without manual steps.

## How to restart (Windows)

```powershell
Get-Process -Name "WeatherAlert.TrayPopup.App" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Stop-Process -Force
dotnet run --project src/WeatherAlert.TrayPopup.App/WeatherAlert.TrayPopup.App.csproj -c Release
```

Run `dotnet run` in the **background** (tray app stays running).

If the process name differs, also stop orphaned `dotnet` hosts that are running this project (check cwd or command line), but prefer stopping by `WeatherAlert.TrayPopup.App` first.

## When to restart

- **Do restart**: feature changes, bug fixes, XAML/UI updates, services wired in `Program.cs`, appsettings behavior changes.
- **Skip restart**: docs-only, comments-only, test-only changes with no runtime impact, or the user explicitly says not to restart.

